  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that Epiquinamide may interact with UDP-glucuronosyltransferase 2B4 through multiple indirect pathways. The first pathway involves Epiquinamide targeting WM-115, which is a substrate of [(2S,5S)-5-(6-aminopurin-9-yl)-3-(hydroxymethyl)-2-methyl-tetrahydrofuran-3-yl]methanol, a compound that directly targets UDP-glucuronosyltransferase 2B4. The second pathway links Epiquinamide to Isobutyl hexanoate, which also targets UDP-glucuronosyltransferase 2B4. The third pathway involves Epiquinamide interacting with Sodium/calcium exchanger 1, which is a target of Cinnabaramide C, another compound that ultimately affects UDP-glucuronosyltransferase 2B4. These findings collectively indicate that Epiquinamide may modulate UDP-glucuronosyltransferase 2B4 through various molecular mechanisms, possibly by influencing the activity or expression of its targets. The scores from the different paths suggest a moderate level of confidence in this relationship, though further experimental validation would be necessary to confirm the direct interaction between Epiquinamide and UDP-glucuronosyltransferase 2B4.",
